<!-- Only text is translated : players, duration, age... are inherited from hearts.game. -->

# Overview

A classic trick-taking game where you try *not* to win certain cards.
Every heart costs you a point and the queen of spades costs a lot,
unless you're bold enough to take them all.

# In short {#summary}

Deal all the cards. On each [[trick]], follow suit if you can.
Avoid taking hearts and the queen of spades: the game ends at 100 points, and the lowest score wins.

# Components

- 1x [[deck]] — standard 52 cards, no jokers
- 1x [[score pad]] and a pencil

> Our 2 of diamonds is bent: use it as the removed card for 3 players.

# Goal

! Have the **fewest** points when someone reaches 100.

# Setup

1. {3p} Remove the 2 of diamonds from the [[deck]].
2. {5p} Remove the 2 of diamonds and the 2 of clubs from the [[deck]].
3. Deal all cards: {3p: 17 | 4p: 13 | 5p: 10} cards each.

| Players          | 3p | 4p | 5p |
|------------------|----|----|----|
| Cards per player | 17 | 13 | 10 |
| Cards removed    | 1  | 0  | 2  |

## Passing {4p}

Before each hand, every player passes 3 cards: left, right, across, then no pass. Repeat.

## Passing {3,5p}

Before each hand, every player passes 3 cards: left, right, then no pass.

# Play

! Follow suit if you can; otherwise play any card.

- The player holding the {3-4p: 2 | 5p: 3} of clubs leads the first [[trick]].
- On the first trick you may not play a heart or the queen of spades, unless you have nothing else.
- ! Hearts can't be led until [[hearts are broken]].
- The highest card of the led suit wins the trick; its winner leads next.

# Scoring

- ! Each heart: 1 point. Queen of spades: 13 points.
- {+omnibus} The jack of diamonds: -10 points.
- If you take all hearts and the queen of spades, you [[shoot the moon]]:
  you score 0 and everyone else scores 26.

Write each hand's score on the [[score pad]].

! The game ends when a player reaches 100 points. Lowest score wins.

# Glossary

Trick
: One card from each player; the highest card of the led suit takes them all.

Hearts are broken
: A heart has been discarded on an earlier trick, so hearts may now be led.

Shoot the moon
: Taking every heart plus the queen of spades in a single hand.
